P18-V01 request/reply facade export correction:
- Pinned Java 5.5.1 exposes public `RequestCallback` and `MessageUtil.createReplyMessage` APIs. The Producer crate already had Rust equivalents, but the primary `rocketmq-classic` facade did not re-export them.
- Re-exported `RequestCallback`, `create_reply_message`, and `ReplyMessageError` from the facade. Added a facade integration test that imports these names, constructs a reply, and checks the null-request error. Updated the Phase 15 request/reply matrix and appended the bounded disposition to the Phase 6 audit; the full P18-V01 audit remains open.
- Initial focused test compilation exposed that `assert_eq!` required `Message: PartialEq`; changed the error assertion to `matches!` because reply messages intentionally do not implement structural equality.
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic --test request_reply_public_api --locked` — passed (1 test).
- `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` — passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` — passed.
